                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[166] *[Inclosure No. 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rumley, collector,
                        to Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the
                        Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilmington, North
                        Carolina</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-10-04"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">October</hi> 4, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">To Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">George S.
                        Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                    Treasury:</hi></p>
                <p>Assistant Adjutant-General J. W. Taylor, at Atlanta, telegraphs to
                    Lieutenant-Colonel R. T. Frank, in command of troops at Smithville, that the
                    marshal must apply to the authorities at Washington before he can assist him in
                    detaining the Lady Sterling. Marshal, with part customs force, left early this
                    morning for Smithville. The requisite authority, on behalf of the marshal, is
                    respectfully requested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. RUMLEY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
